# ICE CREAM — dev server reset

When the user message is **exactly** `ICE CREAM` or clearly asks to run **ICE CREAM** (case-insensitive), **do this immediately** in the repo root (`POC-Joystie`). Do not ask for confirmation.

## Steps (in order)

1. **Kill port 3000** (PowerShell):

```powershell
$p = Get-NetTCPConnection -LocalPort 3000 -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue | Select-Object -ExpandProperty OwningProcess -Unique
if ($p) { $p | ForEach-Object { Stop-Process -Id $_ -Force -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue } }
```

2. **`npm run build`** — wait until it finishes; if it fails, report the error and **do not** start dev.

3. **`npm run dev`** — run in the **background** (`block_until_ms: 0`); confirm when ready at `http://localhost:3000`.

## Reply

One short line: port cleared, build pass/fail, dev URL. No long explanation unless something failed.

## If webpack / `_next/static` 404 persists after reset

Optionally delete `.next` before step 2, then rebuild and restart dev.

## Not ICE CREAM

Ignore this rule unless the user used the codeword.
